Kakutstha departed Pakashasana tells folded Rama sight not fruitless ask mind desire --- Rama with Lakshmana and Sita asks if pleased make true word to revive monkeys fallen for him --- Rama chooses devoted death-disregarding monkeys to obtain by grace and wishes disease-woundless strong monkeys and bears --- Rama wishes out-of-season chief roots fruits and clear rivers where monkeys stand --- Indra calls it a great boon and says monkeys will rise as from sleep end with kin in supreme joy --- Indra says trees flower-flecked fruitful and rivers water-filled out of season --- Monkeys become woundless wondering at bodies first wounded then healed --- Best gods seeing purpose fulfilled praise praise-worthy Rama with Lakshmana --- Gods bid go to Ayodhya dismiss monkeys console devoted ascetic Mithili see vow-bound Bharata consecrate self and delight citizens --- Bidding farewell gods joyful go to heaven in sunlike vimanas and Rama bows and orders lodging --- Lakshmana-Rama-guarded joyful famed army blazes with fortune everywhere as night led by cool-rayed moon